  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">One Health Knowledge Nexus: generating knowledge and evidence for decision-makers and practitioners</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Given the wide range of potential topics and expertise needed, the One Health Knowledge Nexus (OHKN) aims to bring together a wide network of people for engagement, knowledge exchange, learning, and dissemination to support the further advancement of One Health by addressing the following knowledge and evidence gaps:  

- Intersectoral and integrated health cooperation, governance and implementation remain weak in most countries. 
- The impacts of many pests and diseases and the cost-effectiveness of OH solutions to tackle them remain under-researched.  
- Limited systematic studies of how OH initiatives tackle emerging and other threats and can be scaled. 
- Incomplete understanding of the drivers of spillover of infectious diseases and how they can best be tackled in a One Health approach. 
- Insufficient business plans, prioritization and strategizing for OH policy and planning. 
- Low investment in OH infrastructure, including OH databases, tools, information sharing, strategies, and plans.</narrative>
  </description>
